---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import joshStandingImg from '../assets/images/headshots/josh-standing.jpg';
import concertWideImg from '../assets/images/concert-wide.jpg';
---

<Layout title="About | Josh Turknett, MD" currentPage="about" description="Josh Turknett is a board-certified neurologist, four-time bestselling author, and founder of the Institute for Performance Neurology.">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
        <h1 class="page-hero-title">About Josh</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">I'm a board-certified neurologist, a four-time bestselling author, and the founder of the Institute for Performance Neurology. My work is about how the brain builds extraordinary skill, and how people can use that to learn and perform at their best.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero-photo">
        <Image src={joshStandingImg} width={900} widths={[480, 720, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 90vw, 40vw" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" alt="Josh Turknett" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow fade-in">
      <p class="lead">I spent the first part of my career in clinical neurology and research. My research focused on Alzheimer's disease and cognitive aging. Clinically, I've treated people with memory disorders and complex headache conditions.</p>
      <p>The deeper I went, the more I found myself drawn to the opposite question. Not why brains fail, but how they produce extraordinary capability in the first place, and why we so badly underestimate what every brain can do.</p>
      <p class="list-intro">I found that the most important questions about human potential don't have a field of their own:</p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>How do we build ability?</li>
        <li>How do we use it when the pressure is on?</li>
        <li>How do we keep it for a lifetime?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Educators, sports psychologists, and brain-health researchers each study one piece. Almost none of that work starts with how the brain actually works.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Institute -->
  <section class="section section--gray">
    <div class="container narrow fade-in">
      <h2>The Institute for Performance Neurology</h2>
      <p>I founded the Institute for Performance Neurology to study those three questions together, starting with the brain. We call that work Performance Neurology: the science of how people build, use, and keep their abilities across a lifetime.</p>
      <a href="https://performanceneurology.institute" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="small-link">Visit the Institute →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Brainjo -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split split--reverse">
        <div class="split-image fade-in">
          <Image src={concertWideImg} width={1200} widths={[600, 900, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Josh Turknett performing" />
        </div>
        <div class="split-content fade-in fade-in-delay-1">
          <h2>Brainjo</h2>
          <p>Brainjo started as an experiment. I wanted to see whether learning science could help adults learn music by removing the obstacles that make most of them quit.</p>
          <p>It grew into a method that thousands of adult learners around the world have used. And it keeps showing the same thing: when an adult struggles to learn, the fix is almost always in how they practice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick facts -->
  <section class="section section--gray">
    <div class="container narrow fade-in">
      <h2>Quick facts</h2>
      <ul class="fact-list">
        <li>Board-certified neurologist</li>
        <li>Four-time bestselling author: <em>The Genius and the Impostor</em>, <em>Anyone Can Play Music</em> (first published as <em>The Laws of Brainjo</em>), <em>The Migraine Miracle</em>, and <em>Keto for Migraine</em></li>
        <li>Founder of the Institute for Performance Neurology</li>
        <li>Creator of Brainjo, the music-learning method</li>
        <li>Host of the Performance Neurology Podcast, and co-host of the Better Brain Fitness podcast with Dr. Tommy Wood</li>
        <li>Writer of <a href="https://joshturknett.substack.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brains, Banjos &amp; Beyond</a>, a weekly newsletter with more than 50,000 readers</li>
        <li>Award-winning banjo player, with wins in banjo and string band contests</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="/books" class="cta">See the books</a>
        <a href="/speaking" class="cta cta--outline">Book a talk</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
